properties.description:
Drives the MCP surface the way a caller does. It covers:
- objection standing: an unestablished objection contests (proof status contested, and a step resting on the claim reads unknown, never broken); a reply that holds answers it; an established counterexample refutes; two claims that object to each other are both contested;
- a contested Decision governing both sides of a dispute: it suppresses the contradiction defect and is counted in swept.suppressed_by_held_open;
- reasoning_report end to end: roots, rests_on, uncited_premises, warrants, objection standing, cited sources, still_contested, unsupported and what_this_means;
- reading one claim reads only what is under it;
- a design with no reasoning says so, and a claim no node holds is refused.
